# Denali Gravity remediation

## Problem

**Denali** is the G3 reference workspace (deep operator/guest/finance), and
**Harbor** is now the second certified product family at G1 guest-only. Urban,
starter, and guest-club remain stubs/scaffolds. Finance-ws2/3/4/6 are
registry-only fixtures; finance-ws5 and booking-ws2 are supported capability
proofs, not certified guest product families.

Full inventory, hostile review, and phase map:

[`denali-gravity-remediation-map.mdoc`](./denali-gravity-remediation-map.mdoc)
(promoted from local scratch in PSR-2b; rev 2).

**PSR-4a export classification (2026-07-31):** every Denali `package.json` export
is classified and cohorted for deprecation without deletion — see
[`psr-4a-denali-export-classification.mdoc`](../audits/snapshots/2026-07-31/psr-4a-denali-export-classification.mdoc)
(14 public-contract ≤15; 39 host-private, −9 vs ≤30 target; 80 shrink-candidates
as discovery only).

## Two paths (do not conflate)

| Path | Meaning | Program |
| ---- | ------- | ------- |
| **A — Second club** | New tenant on certified `denali` | P10 / Phase H — keep green |
| **B — Second product family** | New workspace type without Denali fork | This remediation (DG-*) |

## Ownership buckets

| Bucket | Owner | Rule |
| ------ | ----- | ---- |
| **P-contract** | `workspace-sdk` (+ codegen) | Ports, shared types, compose contracts — no product literals |
| **P-lib** | SDK subpaths / future neutral guest-http package | Helpers imported by ≥2 workspace handlers — no `pluginId` branches |
| **C** | `workspace.manifest.json` | Prefixes, presentation, theme, SEO, tiers |
| **W** | `packages/workspaces/<id>` | Thin handlers + domain schema/UI/rules — keep `handlerPackage` on workspace |

**Forbidden:** moving workspace HTTP handlers into `apps/api`. Hosts stay loader/codegen-only.

## Product maturity ladder

| Rung | Name | DG exit |
| ---- | ---- | ------- |
| G0 | Scaffold | — |
| G1 | Guest-viable (catalog + register + landing) | DG-4 |
| G2 | Operator-viable | optional before certify |
| G3 | Reference-class (Denali today) | not required for product #2 day-one |

## DG-0 locks (working defaults — 2026-07-31)

| ID | Lock |
| -- | ---- |
| OD-1 | Product #2 vehicle = **1b new `pluginId`**; Urban remains Phase 7 proof |
| OD-2 | P-lib home starts as **`@app-tour/workspace-sdk` `./http` subpath**; promote to dedicated package only if surface grows |
| OD-5 | Certify target = **G1 or G2**, not Denali G3 parity |
| OD-6 | Path B proceeds unless Architect cancels for brand-only Path A |

## Phase order (serialized)

```text
DG-0 (this doc) → DG-1 P-lib + guest-club consumer
                → DG-2 config/catalog neutrality (starter alias **DG-2.1** + profile example **DG-2.2**)
                → DG-3 Denali peel (after consumer #1 green)
                → DG-4 G1 product #2 stub (**DG-4.0** `harbor` scaffolded)
                → DG-5 certify (OD-5)
                → DG-F finance route neutrality (optional)
                → DG-6 cleanup
```

## DG-1 spike (slices 1.1–1.7 landed — further peel still open)

### Goal

Collapse the smallest true clones onto P-contract/P-lib without touching Denali catalog depth.

### Deliverables

1. **`WorkspaceHttpMethod`** — single SoT in `workspace-sdk` (`src/http` + root barrel export; `package.json` `./http` subpath for nodenext). Workspace manifests re-export from `@app-tour/workspace-sdk` (classic `moduleResolution` cannot resolve subpaths yet).
2. **Guest JSON HTTP helpers** — `sendWorkspaceJson` / `readWorkspaceJsonBody` / stub/not-found helpers; **guest-club** is consumer #1.
3. **`assertWorkspaceOwnerMutation`** — generic owner-gate helper; urban + denali thin wrappers call it (shared core; product `canPerform` + error factory stay in W).

**Spike status DG-1.1 (2026-07-31):** deliverables 1–3 implemented + SDK unit tests green; guest-club build/test green; denali `tsc --noEmit` green; urban build green. Urban `REQ-P7-007` may fail if **pre-existing** `platform-core` dirty tree drifts the Phase 7 digest — not caused by this SDK P-lib (DG-1 does not edit `platform-core`).

