### DG-4.7 slice — live G1 E2E harbor (Architect YES)

**Gate:** Architect **YES** for live G1 E2E (2026-07-31).

**Goal:** marketing catalog → portal register for `harbor` smoke tenant (DG-4 exit criterion).

**Prerequisites / fixes in-slice**

1. Export `buildHarborEventJsonLd` (guest-seo guard + fixture).
2. Harbor package `./host/*` export aliases (codegen `register-harbor` imports).
3. `HarborIntakeStep` POSTs `/api/catalog/registrations` (guest-club parity).
4. `apps/api` depends on `@app-tour/workspace-harbor` + `HANDLER_DISPATCH_KIND` bare/product-param for harbor.
5. Smoke servers + Playwright: catalog browse/city/detail + register CTA → OTP → intake → success.
6. Hook id **SMK-MKT-HARBOR-01** (local command; optional yaml later).

**01c failure modes (observed) → fixes**

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Portal register shows `REGISTRATION_CLOSED` / missing phone step | (1) Harbor steps lacked `"use client"` (Denali parity). (2) Even when server `registerWorkspacePluginSafe` returns `ready` with flow+steps populated, `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` (`"use client"`) reads a **separate** webpack client-layer registry Map — empty → closed. | Add `"use client"` on harbor steps; portal `ensureHarborRegistrationFlowClient()` (sync, client-layer) so the client webpack registry Map is filled before `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` reads steps. |
| `Blocked cross-origin request from portal.harbor.localhost to /_next/*` | Canonical local portal is `portal.{club}.localhost` (PCMS-COOK-03). Next `allowedDevOrigins` had only `*.portal.localhost` (legacy inverted), not `portal.*.localhost`. | Add `portal.*.localhost` (+ explicit `portal.denali.localhost` for G-P6-UI-08). |
| `MISSING_MESSAGE: …REGISTRATION_CLOSED` | Closed-flow alert key existed only as `URBAN_REGISTRATION_CLOSED`. | Add `REGISTRATION_CLOSED` to en/fa `catalogRegistration` messages. |

**Verify:** `PW_NO_REUSE_SERVER=1 pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test:smoke:harbor` (API+portal+marketing).

**Spike status DG-4.7 (2026-07-31):** **GREEN** — SMK-MKT-HARBOR-01a/b/c **3/3** (~50s). Fixes: harbor `"use client"` steps · portal `allowedDevOrigins` includes `portal.*.localhost` · `REGISTRATION_CLOSED` i18n · portal `ensureHarborRegistrationFlowClient()` fills the **client-layer** registration registry (RSC register alone is insufficient). DG-4 G1 E2E exit criterion met.

**Not in this slice:** DG-5 certify · DG-3 peel · full guest-hooks yaml matrix expansion · Postgres store.

### DG-4.7.1 slice — client-layer registration ensure (Path A harden)

**Gap after DG-4.7:** `ensureHarborRegistrationFlowClient` was harbor-only. `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` is shared — Denali / Urban / guest-club hit the same RSC vs client webpack registry split. Path A (Denali marketing→portal register) would regress to `REGISTRATION_CLOSED` without a matching client-layer ensure.

**Logic**

1. Own the ensure in `guest-workspace-runtime` (same package as `register-*.generated`) as a `"use client"` switch: `ensureWorkspaceRegistrationFlowClient(pluginId)`.
2. Portal flow calls that helper for every workspace (not harbor special-case).
3. Per-plugin ensure mirrors generated full registrar **intake + flow graph** (intake plugin registry + surface + steps; Denali also runs transport initializer). Missing intake → `INTAKE_PLUGIN_NOT_REGISTERED` on Denali intake render.
4. Add `"use client"` to guest-club + urban intake/done steps (Denali/harbor already have it).

**Verify (targeted, no full gate):**

```text
PW_NO_REUSE_SERVER=1 pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test:smoke:harbor
PW_NO_REUSE_SERVER=1 pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test:smoke   # Path A Denali SMK-MKT-03
```


**Path A follow-through (same slice):** Denali intake now renders after client ensure; remaining smoke failure was API `MEMBERSHIP_NOT_FOUND` on guest-sentinel `saveGuestProfileFields` when portal BFF lacked a matching session user. Guard: skip profile persist when `guestUserId === WORKSPACE_PUBLIC_CATALOG_GUEST_USER_ID`; Denali intake `fetch` uses `credentials: "same-origin"`.

**Spike status DG-4.7.1 (2026-07-31):** **GREEN for Path A catalog+register** — harbor smoke still **3/3**; Denali **SMK-MKT-03** green after client ensure (intake+flow) + guest-sentinel profile-persist guard. P3-E2E-D01 still fails later on `[data-portal-member-registrations]` (/me member module — beyond Path A catalog+register checklist; likely session/cookie for L4 member surface when registration used guest sentinel).

**Not in this slice:** DG-3 domain peel · DG-5 certify · codegen of ensure modules · D01 /me member-module session harden.

### DG-4.7.2 slice — Path A D01 /me session JWT parity

**Symptom (P3-E2E-D01):** After success CTA → `http://portal.operator.localhost:3003/me/registrations`, Playwright lands on `/login?portalReturn=/me/registrations` and Next renders **404** (`This page could not be found`). Registration itself (OTP → intake → `POST /api/catalog/registrations` 201) succeeds.

**Root-cause chain**

```text
register-complete Set-Cookie Domain=operator.localhost  (cookie lands in jar)
        │
        ▼
hydrate fetch GET /api/me/profile
        │
        ▼
middleware validateSessionTokenAsync → invalid_signature
        │
        ▼
clearSessionCookieOnResponse (host-only + Domain=operator.localhost)
        │
        ▼
click /me → no session → redirect /login
        │
        ▼
login page fetchCatalogTour(denali login tour …0220) on operator tenant …0014 → null → notFound()
```

**Why `invalid_signature`:** `resolveSmokeApiJwtEnv()` mints **ephemeral** RS256 keys per smoke run. `smoke-marketing-e2e-servers.mjs` spreads `jwtEnv` into **API** only. Portal inherits the parent shell `AUTH_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` (mismatched). Harbor smoke already spreads `jwtEnv` into `portalEnv` — Denali marketing smoke did not.

**Login 404 (secondary):** `resolveMemberLoginCatalogTourId("denali")` → `…0220` (denali.club / tenant `…0003` seed). Operator smoke tenant `…0014` owns `…0210` only. Unauthenticated `/login` therefore 404s even when redirect is intentional. With JWT parity, D01 never needs `/login` after register-complete.

**Fix**

1. Spread `...jwtEnv` into `portalEnv` in `apps/marketing/scripts/smoke-marketing-e2e-servers.mjs` (parity with harbor + `smoke-portal-e2e-servers.mjs`).
2. Keep login-tour / notFound harden as a follow-up if unauthenticated `/login` on operator host must work without a session.

**Verify (targeted):**

```text
PW_NO_REUSE_SERVER=1 pnpm --filter @apps/marketing exec playwright test \
  -c playwright.marketing.config.ts -g 'SMK-MKT-03|P3-E2E-D01 marketing'
PW_NO_REUSE_SERVER=1 pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test:smoke:harbor
```

**Spike status DG-4.7.2 (2026-07-31):** **GREEN** — `P3-E2E-D01` + `SMK-MKT-03` **2/2** (~54s) after `jwtEnv` portal parity. `/me/registrations` returns 200 with session; `GET /api/me/profile` 200 after register-complete (no cookie clear). Harbor smoke regression **3/3**.

### DG-4.7.3 slice — login host tour miss harden (Path A)

**Gap:** Unauthenticated `/login?portalReturn=…` on operator smoke (`pluginId=denali`, tenant `…0014`) calls `notFound()` when `resolveMemberLoginCatalogTourId("denali")` → `…0220` is absent (that id is denali.club / tenant `…0003`). Member-login egress only needs `tourId`/`tourTitle` as flow context for the OTP modal — a missing catalog row must not 404 the login host.

**Fix:** If `fetchCatalogTour` returns null on `/login`, render with fallback title (`tour.title` → branding `displayName` → `pluginId` → `"Tour"`). Keep configured `tourId` for egress. Do **not** change the denali→`…0220` map (still correct for denali.club).

**Verify:** static inspection + `apps/portal/test/portal-member-login-page.spec.ts` (PCMS-LOGIN-01b).

