**Status DG-6.8 (2026-07-31):** Harbor and future guest scaffolds match the
workspace export-surface covenant.

### DG-6.9 slice — close full guest-conformance gaps

The first full guest-conformance run after DG guard wiring found two latent
gaps:

1. Harbor registration flow still implemented merge/transition locally instead
   of delegating to `applyCatalogRegistrationFlowEvent`.
2. `guard-guest-consumer-deps` only recognized inline `pnpm --filter` prebuilds,
   while API prebuild now delegates to `scripts/ci/build-api-workspace-deps.sh`,
   which intentionally builds every workspace via non-no-op `pnpm --dir`.

Harbor now uses the canonical state transition helper. The consumer-dependency
guard accepts the delegated prebuild only after structurally verifying its
all-workspace loop and `pnpm --dir "$dir" run build` command; otherwise it keeps
the former per-package filter checks.

**Status DG-6.9 (2026-07-31):** registration state is single-SoT and the build
dependency guard matches the stronger current CI implementation.

